.TH SDL_HINT_VIDEO_OFFSCREEN_SAVE_FRAMES 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_VIDEO_OFFSCREEN_SAVE_FRAMES \- A variable controlling whether the offscreen video driver saves output frames.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_VIDEO_OFFSCREEN_SAVE_FRAMES \(dqSDL_VIDEO_OFFSCREEN_SAVE_FRAMES\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This only saves frames that are generated using software rendering, not accelerated OpenGL rendering\[char46]
.PP

\(bu \(dq0\(dq: Video frames are not saved to disk\[char46] (default)
.PP
\(bu \(dq1\(dq: Video frames are saved to files in the format
.BR "" \(dq SDL_windowX -Y\[char46]bmp\(dq,
where X is the window ID, and Y is the frame number\[char46]
.PP
This hint can be set anytime\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

